    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d570">

                <pb facs="0685" n="673" xml:id="pg673"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">845.00/1359a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Officer in Charge at New
                        Delhi</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Merrell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-06-16T15:00:00-04:00">June 16, 1942—3 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>279. It is imperative that the Department be kept as fully informed as possible
                    regarding all factors affecting the internal security situation in India. A
                    telegraphic report outlining the situation as perceived at present by you should
                    be submitted. Your appraisal of the situation should be cabled at weekly
                    intervals thereafter, with particular reference to such developments as may be
                    occurring in connection with Gandhi’s threatened mass civil disobedience. Any
                    information of special significance should of course be reported:
                    immediately.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
